Release 4.7.1.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 11:56:40

Release 4.7.0.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 11:10:14

Added. The Refresh row is now the Screen row. It shows the resolution, scale and refresh rate of the screen the
window is on, as the desktop reports them. A Refresh row you hid stays hidden as the Screen row. The wiki's table
names the new row. test_overlay.py checks the new value.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 21:12:00

Release 4.6.2.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 20:42:13

Fixed. The text of the wiki chapter, the README, the overlay's tooltips, the --native-wayland help and the module notes
is rewritten in short, plain sentences. The README's link now names BC-250 System Overlay in the wiki. The wiki said
four rows need the bc250_vrm module. It is five: CPU rail, GPU rail, 12 V input, CPU VRM temp and GPU VRM temp. The GPU
row's tooltip now names GPU Manager, where the old text said the governor app. Nothing the app does has changed. No test
changed.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 19:56:43

Release 4.6.1.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 18:45:01

Fixed. The GPU row showed the whole chip's power as the GPU's. It now shows the GPU's own power, from the voltage
regulator, with Quickfix's VRM Sensors on, and none without. A new row Chip power holds the GPU driver's value: CPU,
GPU and the rest together.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 15:13:54

Release 4.6.0.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 14:24:02

Added. A row 12 V input: the board's 12 V input as the voltage regulator measures it, with Quickfix's VRM Sensors on.
It is a dash without the module, as the other rows of the regulator are.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 12:24:43

Release 4.5.0.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 00:56:48

Release 4.4.0.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 00:38:50

Added. The tooltip of the four bc250_vrm rows names BC-250 Quickfix's VRM Sensors, which loads the module.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 23:06:26

Added. Four rows that the bc250_vrm kernel module fills: CPU rail and GPU rail (voltage, current and power), CPU VRM
temp and GPU VRM temp. Without the module they show a dash and a tooltip that says why.

